  "claims": [
    "Strict successful feedback requires current captured request identity, un-aborted state and exact server exercise/revision/requested-metric/engine-metric echoes.",
    "Strict accepted guidance is bound to current request, education generation, behavior token, exercise/revision and requested metric.",
    "Stale or aborted feedback and old metric responses are rejected by the model; AST presentation has no canonical correspondence.",
    "Legacy missing feedback echoes and missing guidance metric are concrete accepted counterexamples to the stronger strict contract; the strengthened model rejects both.",
    "Logical metric-indexed cache keys separate metrics; actual serialized key correspondence is unproved."
  ],
